  "id": "speech-impairment",
  "term": "speech impairment",
  "definition": "Speech impairment is a difficulty with producing spoken sounds, including problems with pronunciation, articulation, fluency, or phonation, that can reduce how effectively a person communicates. Because speech is important for communication and children’s logical and social development, identifying these difficulties early can help improve outcomes.",
